@meta
id: 05-09
title: Counting words instead of pressing
chapter: 05
type: lesson
skills: word-counts, word-w
par: 18
minutes: 4
vscode: Ctrl-Right nine times, or give up and click
open: refunds.md

@brief
Chapter four taught you that `5j` beats holding `j`. The same count goes
in front of every word motion, and for the same reason: one considered
number instead of a burst of presses you have to watch.

`3w` is three words forward. `2b` is two back. `4e` is four word-ends
forward.

The nightly job is specifically the payment reconciliation job. Make the
first line read:

    Refund requests are queued and processed by the nightly payment reconciliation job.

Par is tight enough that pressing `w` nine times will not fit.

@keys
| `3w` | three words forward |
| `2b` | two words back |
| `4e` | four word-ends forward |
| `i` | insert before the cursor |

@hints
Count the words between where you are and where `payment` needs to go.
Your finger does not need to count them one press at a time.
--
A number typed before a motion repeats it. The digits go first: type the
count, then the motion key, and nothing happens until the key lands.
--
It is nine words from the start of the line to `reconciliation`. `9w`,
then `i`, type `payment` and a space, `Esc`, `:wq`.

@solution
    9w  i payment <Esc>  :wq<Enter>

Sixteen keystrokes against twenty-three for the same edit done by
hammering `w`, and the count version is the one you can trust. Counting
nine words feels slow the first few times and then it does not, in
exactly the way counting lines stopped feeling slow last chapter.

Two things make the count worth the thought. The first is that it is one
decision instead of nine — you look, you count, you go, and you are not
monitoring the cursor while it travels. The second matters more later:
when a count is attached to a motion and the motion is attached to an
operator, the whole thing becomes one undoable action. Chapter eight
turns that into `d3w` and it only works because the count lives on the
motion.

If nine is more than you can count at a glance, that is a signal the
motion is wrong, not that the count is. A target that far away usually
wants `W`, a search, or a different line entirely.

@start refunds.md
Refund requests are queued and processed by the nightly reconciliation job.
Anything queued after 23:00 waits for the following night.

@expected refunds.md
Refund requests are queued and processed by the nightly payment reconciliation job.
Anything queued after 23:00 waits for the following night.
